       ddppkkgg--ddiivveerrtt [_o_p_t_i_o_n...]  _c_o_m_m_a_n_d

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddppkkgg--ddiivveerrtt is the utility used to set up and update the list of
       diversions.

       File _d_i_v_e_r_s_i_o_n_s are a way of forcing ddppkkgg(1) not to install a file into
       its location, but to a _d_i_v_e_r_t_e_d location. Diversions can be used
       through the Debian package scripts to move a file away when it causes a
       conflict. System administrators can also use it to override some
       package's configuration file, or whenever some files (which aren't
       marked as “conffiles”) need to be preserved by ddppkkgg, when installing a
       newer version of a package which contains those files.

